A minimal CAS-based spinlock:

```c
void acquire(atomic_int *lock) {
    int expected = 0;
    while (!atomic_compare_exchange_weak(lock, &expected, 1)) {
        expected = 0;  // reset for retry after a failed attempt
    }
}

void release(atomic_int *lock) {
    atomic_store(lock, 0);
}
```

Every failed `compare_exchange` means another thread currently holds the lock; the loop just keeps retrying (spinning) rather than yielding the CPU — appropriate only when the expected wait is very short, since spinning burns CPU cycles the whole time.
